  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the following reaction sequence, the amount of <math> <mtext>D</mtext> </math> (in g) formed from <math> <mrow> <mn>10</mn></mrow> </math> moles of acetophenone is ____.<br >\r\n\r\n(Atomic weights in <math><mtext>g </mtext><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>o</mtext><msup><mrow><mtext>l</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mtext>H</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>C</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>N</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>O</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>B</mtext><mtext>r</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The yield (%) corresponding to the product in each step is given in the parenthesis)<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/124343agofigsfuagos.JPG\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "495",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>molecular weight of<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/fkjdfasjsgfasffdssafdsfasdf.JPG\"/>= 330<br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/qfhbaukasjgfkhasdf.jpg\"/><br/>Weight of 1 mol of 2, 4, 6 tribromoaniline = 330 gm<br/>∴ Weight of 1.5 mol of 2, 4, 6 tribromoaniline = 330 × 1.5 = 495 gm</p>",
